+
 The optional top-level `ai` section of a chain configuration persists only `profiles[]` and `channels[]`. Each profile uses the non-secret `profileId/providerType/baseUrl/model/wireApi/authMode/secretRef` fields and has an independent configuration digest under `proofrail:ai-provider-profile:1\n`. Each `channels[]` entry contains only `channel/profileId`, where channel is one of `agent-runner-cli|sessionbridge-silent|sessionbridge-visible`. Both arrays are lexically ordered by primary key and reject duplicates. Every channel references a declared profile; an unbound channel remains unconfigured and fails closed rather than inheriting another channel. Host authentication cannot carry `secretRef`; secret authentication requires an opaque reference and HTTPS base URL. `config explain` may expose profileId, the profile configuration digest, and channel bindings, but never `secretRef`, credential existence, or any resolved value. Static `validate/config explain/preview` performs no SecretStore read and no availability probe.
 
